<section class="section" style="padding-top:65px"><div class="container docs-layout"><aside class="docs-sidebar"><span class="eyebrow">Docs</span><h4>Integrations</h4><a href="#channels">Lead channels</a><a href="#messaging">Messaging</a><a href="#voice">Voice</a><a href="#calendar">Calendar</a><a href="#api">API & webhooks</a><a href="#security">Security</a></aside><article class="doc-article"><span class="eyebrow">Integration guide</span><h1>Connect your lead ecosystem to Ally.</h1><p class="hero-copy" style="margin:0">The integration layer is designed to bring acquisition sources and operational tools into the same lead identity, conversation history and automation system.</p><h2 id="channels">Lead channels</h2><p>Depending on the configured environment, Ally can connect WhatsApp, Meta/Facebook, Instagram, Google and Google Ads, website forms, landing pages, voice, phone/SMS, email, chat and other third-party lead platforms.</p><div class="cards"><article class="card"><h3>Meta</h3><p>Bring campaign leads into qualification and immediate conversation workflows.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Google</h3><p>Connect acquisition activity to lead capture, AI engagement and appointments.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Website</h3><p>Use forms, landing pages and chat to create structured enquiries.</p></article></div><h2 id="messaging">Messaging</h2><p>Messaging channels can be connected to the unified inbox so agents and people can work from the same customer context. WhatsApp workflows can include templates, follow-ups, assignments, notifications and approved business messaging.</p><h2 id="voice">Voice</h2><p>Voice integrations can support inbound answering, outbound campaigns, AI qualification, call summaries, analysis and authorized human transfer.</p><h2 id="calendar">Calendar</h2><p>Appointment workflows can use calendar availability for booking, reminders, rescheduling and cancellation handling.</p><h2 id="api">API & webhooks</h2><p>Use APIs and webhooks to connect external lead sources, trigger workflows and synchronize supported CRM events. Production endpoints and authentication details belong to the authenticated Ally environment and should be documented against the deployed backend.</p><div class="code">External lead source
  → webhook / API
  → Ally lead identity
  → AI agent workflow
  → CRM + pipeline
  → human or automated action</div><h2 id="security">Security</h2><p>Keep access tokens, webhook secrets and provider credentials in server-side configuration. Use HTTPS for production integrations, apply role-based access, restrict channel permissions and review integration activity through administrative controls.</p></article></div></section><?php include __DIR__.'/../includes/footer.php'; ?>